From 377f982e179d71f8d174ce6779b2db48d1222dc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:53:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: web API: say that the connection is closed

The web server runs without keep-alive: it closes the connection after
every response. The responses the app writes itself (the API and the old
controllers) are HTTP/1.1 with a Content-Length and no Connection header,
which a client reads as "the connection stays open". A browser then
sends its next request on the connection the server has just closed and
that request fails (quick clicks on the Floppy page: "Lost connection").

Every response the app writes now carries "Connection: close".
